Find My rolling-key implementation provenance
============================================

FindMyCrypto.cpp adapts the rolling-key arithmetic/X9.63 sequence inspected in:
- VibeCoderLab/esp32-findmy-integration
  commit 1c0ede3989ee11bd97e9bed169a7fbc6a99db460
  firmware/src/main.cpp (not firmware/main.cpp, which does not exist at that pin).
- parawanderer/FindMy.py
  commit 7969003ca785658369b650f75d9e7ca519566bf6
  findmy/util/crypto.py and findmy/accessory.py; this is the dependency pinned by
  the above project's sources.lock.json.

The portable scheduling/persistence API and host tests are new code. No upstream
Arduino/Bluedroid globals or controller lifecycle have been imported. The packet
layout was compared against the MIT firmware above. This is source-informed,
not a claim of formal clean-room implementation or Apple certification.

